            "type": "target",
            "value": "5",
          },
          {
            "id": "o4",
            "inStrip": false,
            "label": "monthly orders",
            "type": "target",
            "value": "+30%",
          },
        ],
        "overview": {
          "company": "Sri Mandir",
          "kind": "study",
          "summary": "WhatsApp-native puja booking with AI recommendations and spiritual calendar to increase repeat devotion",
          "title": "Puja engagement platform",
          "topics": [
            "CRM",
            "Personalization",
            "Monetization",
            "Engagement",
            "Prototyping",
          ],
        },
        "schemaVersion": 1,
        "seo": {},
        "settings": {
          "redirectOldSlug": false,
        },
        "story": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Improve the <strong>order per user (Monthly order frequency)</strong> for the puja service at Sri Mandir.</p>",
                "id": "c01-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c01",
            "title": "Assignment Objective",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Core Puja Performance is Authentic:</strong> We assume the religious rituals are performed authentically by verified priests according to scriptures, and the challenge lies in communicating and ensuring this authenticity in the online format.</li><li><strong>Technological Infrastructure:</strong> Sri Mandir possesses or can acquire the necessary technological infrastructure to implement proposed digital enhancements, including localisation.</li><li><strong>Access to User Data:</strong> Basic user data regarding puja bookings, frequency, location (inferred), and stated preferences is accessible for analysis and personalisation efforts.</li><li><strong>Motivation Beyond One-Time Need:</strong> While specific needs might drive initial bookings, there's an underlying desire among users for ongoing spiritual connection, seeking blessings, and performing religious duties regularly.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c02-b1",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c02",
            "title": "Assumptions",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "columns": 3,
                "id": "c03-b1",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "Individuals who integrate technology into their lives and seek convenient ways to practice faith.",
                    "title": "Tech-Savvy Devotees (Millennials & Gen Z)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Those living away from their preferred temples or countries, seeking to stay connected to their spiritual roots.",
                    "title": "NRIs & Geographically Distant Devotees",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Users with busy schedules who prioritise efficiency — seeking convenience & accessibility to easily book and participate from home.",
                    "title": "Time-Constrained Individuals",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Users booking for particular life events, astrological reasons, or personal challenges.",
                    "title": "Individuals with Specific Needs",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Tech-comfortable individuals who value consistency in spiritual rituals and seek regular puja participation.",
                    "title": "Tech-informed Devotees Seeking Regular Practice",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Older, tradition-focused individuals deeply devoted to puja but less comfortable with digital tools. Typically use WhatsApp or Facebook. May struggle with online payments.",
                    "title": "Non-Technological Regular Devotees",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "A potentially underserved segment comfortable in regional Indian languages.",
                    "title": "Non-Hindi/English Speaking Devotees",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c03",
            "title": "Target User Segments",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Key Motivations",
                "id": "c04-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Spiritual Connection & Fulfillment:</strong> Seeking blessings and maintaining religious practice. Staying connected to traditional roots — often through listening to aartis and bhajans.</li><li><strong>Convenience & Accessibility:</strong> Booking and participating from anywhere, anytime.</li><li><strong>Time & Effort Saving:</strong> Avoiding logistical hassles of offline pujas.</li><li><strong>Authenticity & Trust (Desired):</strong> Expectation that rituals are performed correctly by qualified priests.</li><li><strong>Bridging Distance:</strong> Connecting with specific temples or traditions from afar.</li><li><strong>Receiving Prasad & Blessings:</strong> The tangible outcome of the puja.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Pain Points (from Google Play Reviews & App Usage)",
                "id": "c04-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Lack of Personalisation & Context:</strong> The puja service page is generic, lacking recommendations based on user history, preferences, or local relevance (e.g., what others are booking in that location).</li><li><strong>Product Education:</strong> Low awareness & discoverability of the Puja service and its offerings.</li><li><strong>Lack of Trust Signals:</strong> Absence of trust on online payments. No social proofing (e.g., how many users viewed/booked). Concerns about divine box quality and missing items. Lack of clarity on puja venue. Critical issue of incorrect Gotra being used. Insufficient communication regarding venue changes or Prasad issues.</li><li><strong>Accessibility Limitations:</strong> Service primarily in Hindi and English alienates users comfortable only in regional languages.</li><li><strong>Learning Curve:</strong> Multiple steps and unfamiliar interactions differ from typical app flows (like FB, WhatsApp), creating a barrier especially for first-time users.</li><li><strong>Lack of Urgency/Timeliness Cues:</strong> No timer on critical pujas where timing is significant to create booking urgency.</li><li><strong>Limited Guidance on Options:</strong> Difficulty identifying the 'most picked plans' or best options without personalisation.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c04",
            "title": "User Motivations & Pain Points",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Opportunities lie in addressing identified pain points to build trust, enhance convenience, and create a more personalised and engaging experience that encourages repeat and more frequent bookings.</p>",
                "id": "c05-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Build and Communicate Trust:</strong> Proactively address concerns about authenticity, Prasad, Gotra, and venue transparency.</li><li><strong>Enhance Personalisation & Relevance:</strong> Make the puja discovery and booking process highly relevant based on profile, history, and context (location, auspicious dates).</li><li><strong>Product Education:</strong> Build awareness & product education experience for users.</li><li><strong>Subscriptions:</strong> Offer easy ways to book recurring pujas and manage spiritual obligations.</li><li><strong>Improve Accessibility:</strong> Cater to users in their preferred language & community (e.g., Bihari, Bengali).</li><li><strong>Optimise for Conversion:</strong> Use urgency cues wherever appropriate to reduce booking time.</li><li><strong>Improve Post-Booking Experience:</strong> Ensure smooth Prasad delivery and clear communication throughout the process.</li><li>Implement robust data collection for Gotra and integrate it clearly into booking and confirmation.</li><li>Develop a personalised dashboard showing recommended pujas, upcoming events, and loyalty status.</li><li>Display social proof metrics (e.g., 'X users viewing,' 'Y users booked this week').</li><li>Offer multiple language selection options for content and communication.</li><li>Streamline the booking flow, clearly presenting options like single booking vs. subscription.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c05",
            "title": "Opportunities for Improvement",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Time-Constrained Professional / Millennial / Gen Z",
                "id": "c06-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Puja Recommendation Engine</li><li>Personalised Spiritual Calendar & Reminders</li><li>Subscription Packages</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> Puja Order ↑ · Subscription Adoption & Renewal % · Reminder Click Rate</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "NRI / Geographically Distant Devotee",
                "id": "c06-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Personalised Recommendations by region/tradition</li><li>Spiritual Calendar with local timezone</li><li>Gift a Puja</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> Repeat Booking Rate from NRIs · Gifting Feature Usage · NRI Engagement %</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Needs-Based / Occasional User",
                "id": "c06-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Problem-Specific Recommendation Engine</li><li>Monthly Curated Focus Pujas</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> Engagement with Focus Pujas · Bounce Rate on Need-Based Pages ↓ · Booking Conversion Rate ↑</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b6",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Tech-informed Devotees Seeking Regular Practice",
                "id": "c06-b7",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Subscription Packages</li><li>Personalised Spiritual Calendar & Reminders</li><li>Tiered Loyalty Rewards</li><li>Puja & Aashirvaad Box Authenticity</li><li>Complementary Puja Suggestions</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> Puja Users ↑ · Puja Booked ↑ · Loyalty Program Participation · Subscription Adoption & Renewal % · # Puja Box Complaints</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b8",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Non-Technological Regular Devotees",
                "id": "c06-b9",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Product Education</li><li>Video feed of puja, chadhavs or rituals</li><li>WhatsApp Integration</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> Engagement Rate on Education · Video View Count · Engagement & retention on video feed · Conversion Rate via WhatsApp</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b10",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Skeptical / New Online Puja User",
                "id": "c06-b11",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Post-Puja Transparency (video, photo, prasad)</li><li>Responsive Support</li><li>Social Proofing & User Testimonials</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> First-Time Booking Conversion Rate · Support Ticket Resolution Time ↓ · NPS / CSAT Score ↑</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b12",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Non-Hindi/English Speaking Devotees",
                "id": "c06-b13",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Multi-Language UI & Booking Flow</li><li>Regional Language Video/Audio Mantras</li><li>Local Language Support Team</li><li>Puja Descriptions in Native Tongues</li><li><em>Metrics:</em> Drop-off Rate in Non-Hindi/English Regions ↓ · Increase in Bookings from Vernacular Users · Language Preference Opt-in Rate ↑</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b14",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c06",
            "title": "Proposed Solutions by Segment",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>To boost monthly orders per user, we will prioritise these key segments:</p>",
                "id": "c07-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>1. Time-Constrained Professionals / Millennials / Gen Z:</strong> Their busy, tech-savvy nature makes them highly receptive to convenient, recurring digital solutions like subscriptions, offering the greatest potential for increased monthly frequency.</li><li><strong>2. Tech-informed Devotees Seeking Regular Practice:</strong> Already inclined towards regular practice, they will benefit from streamlined processes, personalisation and subscriptions to maintain or slightly increase their existing high frequency.</li><li><strong>3. Non-Technological Regular Devotees</strong> (like mothers and grandparents): Social media users who struggle with online payments due to trust issues. Their strong religious commitment drives high repeat engagement and potential for increased order frequency.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c07",
            "title": "Priority Segments",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Feature Priority Ranking",
                "id": "c08-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Reach × Impact × Confidence ÷ Effort</p>",
                "id": "c08-b2",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "checkFormula": true,
                "columns": [
                  "#",
                  "Feature",
                  "Reach",
                  "Impact",
                  "Conf.",
                  "Effort",
                  "RICE",
                ],
                "formula": "rice",
                "highlightTop": 3,
                "id": "c08-b3",
                "phoneCards": true,
                "reviewed": [],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "1",
                    "WhatsApp Integration",
                    "9",
                    "2.5",
                    "85%",
                    "2 mo",
                    "9.6",
                  ],
                  [
                    "2",
                    "Product Education",
                    "7",
