Word Trip baseline comparable",
                    "title": "ARPU",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c02",
            "title": "Competitive Landscape",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Based on observations from Word Trip & competitor app usage over multiple days:</p>",
                "id": "c03-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "1. High Onboarding Friction",
                "id": "c03-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Word Trip shows 3 consecutive pop-ups (thank you message, iOS ads tracking, notifications) before even asking for login/account creation — then lands on the first product experience. This creates <strong>5+ clicks before first gameplay</strong>, the highest among all competitors.</li><li><strong>How competitors do it differently:</strong> Word Escapes: only EULA acceptance before product demo. Word Connect: iOS ad tracking then immediately starts gameplay. Word Cookies: just two pop-ups before gameplay.</li><li><strong>Why this matters:</strong> First-time UX directly impacts install-to-player conversion. Each additional click before gameplay increases drop-off by ~20% (GameAnalytics). Acquisition costs are wasted when users abandon before experiencing core gameplay. High friction creates negative first impressions leading to poor store ratings.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c03-b3",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "2. Limited Game Formats",
                "id": "c03-b4",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Word Trip offers only <strong>one format of word game</strong> unlocked at initial level. The travel theme with hidden bonus words is engaging but becomes repetitive without alternative modes.</li><li><strong>How competitors do it differently:</strong> Zynga Word With Friends: multiple game modes accessible at all levels — daily puzzle, match of the day, solo challenge, word wheel, social gaming, PvP, crosswords, Clubs. Word Connect: offers sentence completion. Word Escapes: crossword-style gameplay as an alternative format.</li><li><strong>Why this matters:</strong> Different formats appeal to various skill levels and play preferences. Udonis Research shows variety significantly reduces churn by preventing gameplay fatigue. Limited formats restrict session length. Multiple formats create cross-promotion opportunities.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c03-b5",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "3. Suboptimal Monetization & IAP Strategy",
                "id": "c03-b6",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Poor IAP Bundle Design:</strong> Best value packs are hidden; first item (600 INR) is neither popular nor best value. Most popular plan placed in the second fold. No restore plan option or mega sale timer.</li><li><strong>Ad Overload:</strong> Excessive ads during the second session, leading to a frustrating user experience.</li><li><strong>How competitors do it differently:</strong> Word Escapes: better bundling, exclusive time-sensitive bundling at start, red color to highlight value. Zynga: places 'most popular' first, uses time-associated offers with shimmer animation. Word Connect: 'one time offer' creating urgency, restore option. Word Cookies: sale timer, most popular bundles at top.</li><li><strong>Why this matters:</strong> IAP optimization impacts revenue without requiring additional users. Optimal IAP presentation can increase conversion by 25–35% (Liftoff). Early ad bombardment damages retention. Urgency mechanics (timers, limited offers) are proven psychological triggers.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c03-b7",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "4. Missing Retention Mechanisms",
                "id": "c03-b8",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Word Trip lacks <strong>leaderboards, daily/weekly milestones, temporal events</strong> (Holi, Diwali), and social gaming features like PvP. Engagement features like clubs and daily spelling bee only unlock at higher levels.</li><li><strong>How competitors do it differently:</strong> Word Escapes: leaderboards for competitive play. Zynga: leaderboards for global & friends, solo challenge, Clubs at all levels. Word Connect: daily tasks with progress promoting retention. Word Cookies: milestones with reward rates. Word With Friends: daily free claim section improving daily behaviour.</li><li><strong>Why this matters:</strong> Retention is the primary driver of LTV in free-to-play games. GameRefinery research shows games with robust retention features maintain 30–40% higher DAU/MAU ratios. Social features create organic growth. Seasonal events create reasons to return.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c03-b9",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c03",
            "title": "User Pain Points",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Initiative Priority Ranking",
                "id": "c04-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Reach × Impact × Confidence ÷ Effort</p>",
                "id": "c04-b2",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "checkFormula": true,
                "columns": [
                  "#",
                  "Initiative",
                  "Reach",
                  "Impact",
                  "Conf.",
                  "Effort",
                  "RICE",
                ],
                "formula": "rice",
                "highlightTop": 3,
                "id": "c04-b3",
                "phoneCards": true,
                "reviewed": [],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "1",
                    "Streamline Onboarding",
                    "10",
