        ],
        "overview": {
          "company": "Arcana · Workspace",
          "kind": "prototype",
          "prdUrl": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MZGAA0LmIOjF_hVQIMYgjWKM06vQP8Aq66b8-xf2xFQ/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.su9f7jlfuspx",
          "summary": "Bloomberg-style modular launchpad for institutional investors — grid-based workspaces with configurable widgets for real-time market monitoring",
          "title": "Arcana Workspace",
          "topics": [
            "0→1",
            "B2B",
            "Prototyping",
            "Workflows",
            "Fintech",
          ],
        },
        "schemaVersion": 1,
        "seo": {},
        "settings": {
          "redirectOldSlug": false,
        },
        "story": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Institutional investors, analysts & researchers operate in a <strong>high frequency, high cognitive load environment</strong>. Their daily workflow involves simultaneously monitoring live prices, charts, news, alerts, and global market context while switching context across multiple asset classes.</p>",
                "id": "c01-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Fragmented Information</strong> — Prices, charts, news, alerts, and market hours live in separate views. Users must mentally stitch insights together by exploring each view independently.</li><li><strong>High Context Switching Cost</strong> — Switching between workflows (e.g., market open vs research) requires re-navigation. Analysts lose time reconstructing views multiple times a day.</li><li><strong>One-Size-Fits-All Interfaces</strong> — Different users track different assets, regions, and time horizons. A single default layout fails all of them.</li><li><strong>Poor State Persistence</strong> — Users expect their layouts, filters, and configurations to persist across sessions. Without this, they rework the same setup every time they log in.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c01-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c01",
            "title": "Problem Statement",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>A modular workspace increases <strong>product stickiness</strong>. Custom dashboards directly correlate with higher retention and daily engagement by becoming the user’s <strong>first preference</strong> for daily monitoring.</li><li>There is <strong>already a market precedent</strong> set by <strong>Bloomberg Launchpad</strong> — one of the most heavily used terminal features — because it solves this exact problem through customizable, persistent widgets & workspaces.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c02-b1",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c02",
            "title": "Why This Is Worth Solving",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Build <strong>Arcana Workspace</strong> — a modular, <strong>Bloomberg-style Launchpad</strong> that allows users to create, save, and switch between personalised workspaces composed of configurable widgets — optimised for real-time monitoring, clarity, and execution with speed, leading to repeat daily usage.</p>",
                "id": "c03-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c03",
            "title": "Product Vision",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Enable users to build custom workspaces using modular widgets from scratch or premade templates</li><li>Templates are workspace formats with widgets designed for unique use cases (NEWS, Portfolio, Research) — with optional Global Settings that are must-haves (e.g., Portfolio template requires selecting an index/equity to power widgets)</li><li>Support adding, resizing, configuring, and saving widget layouts</li><li>Allow multiple tabs/pages per workspace</li><li>Ability to edit / copy / add / save / share workspace & pages, with fast switching between them</li><li>Preserve widget-level intelligence (e.g., Nvidia selected in index & performance widget persists)</li><li><strong>V1 = Signal intake + context + workflow persistence.</strong> V2 = Outcome measurement (performance, deep analytics, risk, attribution, order execution integration)</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b1",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c04",
            "title": "Goals for V1",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>A Bloomberg Launchpad user typically combines price monitors + charts + news feeds to correlate headlines with price reactions, uses alerts to catch significant moves without continuous hovering, and saves workflows by theme (commodity tracking, earnings day, global markets). This mirrors how users segment their day:</p>",
                "id": "c05-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Morning pre-open scan</strong> — Macro indices, overnight movers, news catch-up</li><li><strong>Live session monitoring</strong> — Real-time price action, alerts firing, chart patterns</li><li><strong>Post-close analysis</strong> — P&L review, sector performance, next-day prep</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c05",
            "title": "Market Research",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>These cover the <strong>core workflows of watching prices & signals</strong> — the top job of users. We are launching the monitoring layer, not the outcome layer.</p>",
                "id": "c06-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 3,
                "id": "c06-b2",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "Most basic, most used — priority 1 for every workflow",
                    "title": "Equity Price Monitor",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Global indices (S&P, Nifty) — macro sentiment gauge widely used by analysts",
                    "title": "Index Tracker",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Critical for cross-asset views (similar to Bloomberg’s commodities widget)",
                    "title": "Commodity Prices",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Visual confirmation of trends & patterns — core to all workflows",
                    "title": "Real-Time Chart",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Provides context to price movements — heavily used across all personas",
                    "title": "Live News Feed",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Simple price threshold alerts — helps catch key events without always watching",
                    "title": "Price Alerts",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Supports a global view across regions and trading sessions",
                    "title": "Timezone / Market Hours",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c06",
            "title": "Prioritised Widgets",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Workspace",
                "id": "c07-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Grid-based canvas (like Metabase dashboard layout) — chosen over free-form positioning to optimise for scale, stability, and cognitive clarity in high-load environments</li><li>Preset templates for core use cases (Portfolio Analysis, Single Stock Analysis, etc.) with pre-specified widgets and optional Global Settings</li><li>Workspaces can be copied, renamed, shared, rearranged, customised and managed from settings</li><li>Added workspaces appear side-by-side and switch instantly on click</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Widgets",
                "id": "c07-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Modular, atomic blocks of the workspace with multiple responsive UI sizes (like Apple widgets — different UI for different grid sizes)</li><li>Can be configured (columns/filters/indicators/flags), added, resized, repositioned, renamed, or removed</li><li>Widgets retain their full capabilities inside the workspace (e.g., Summary widget retains % AUM & % Gross selections)</li><li>Users can add any widget from the terminal directly to a workspace page; widget lands in the next vacant grid area</li><li>Widgets cannot overlap. Option to export widget data in relevant Excel format</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Pages",
                "id": "c07-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Each workspace supports multiple pages representing sub-contexts (e.g., Price, Valuation within a Portfolio template)</li><li>Pages visible side-by-side with add, delete, reorder, rename, copy, share capabilities</li><li>Pages can be managed from settings or via right-click context menu</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b6",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Group Components (V1 → V2)",
                "id": "c07-b7",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>V1: Global Settings for presets — groupings are done during template creation (e.g., selecting a stock links all widgets)</li><li>V2: Fully-fledged Group Manager where users can map components to each other, change a security in one component and all grouped components update</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b8",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c07",
            "title": "Core Capabilities",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "First-Time User Experience",
                "id": "c08-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Entry:</strong> No existing workspaces</p>",
                "id": "c08-b2",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "id": "c08-b3",
                "stages": [
                  {
                    "title": "User opens Arcana Workspace, clicks Create New → 3 options: optimised view for screen, sample view from manager, or blank canvas",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "On blank canvas: Launchpad toolbar appears with Page 1 and no widgets. Search bar available to add components or select templates",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "User adds first component or selects template, configures parameters/global settings, adjusts position & size",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "User saves the view and workspace",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "journey",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Exit:</strong> Saved workspace with at least one page and widget</p>",
                "id": "c08-b4",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Adding & Configuring a Widget",
                "id": "c08-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Entry:</strong> Active workspace with at least one page</p>",
                "id": "c08-b6",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "id": "c08-b7",
                "stages": [
                  {
                    "title": "User clicks search → Component/Template Browser opens with categories and previews",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Selects component → appears on canvas in default state",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "User configures columns/filters/indicators/flags, optionally renames widget",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "A widget can’t exist in the same state twice on a particular page",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "journey",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Exit:</strong> Configured widget on active page</p>",
                "id": "c08-b8",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Building a Multi-Page Workspace",
                "id": "c08-b9",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Entry:</strong> Workspace with at least one saved page</p>",
                "id": "c08-b10",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "id": "c08-b11",
                "stages": [
                  {
                    "title": "User clicks +New Page, creates Page 2 inside the same workspace",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Adds different widgets (e.g., Asia markets) or templates from search",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Right-click options: copy, rename, rearrange, delete, share, customise",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Pages appear side-by-side, switch instantly on click",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "journey",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Exit:</strong> One workspace, multiple task-specific pages</p>",
                "id": "c08-b12",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Returning User Daily Flow",
                "id": "c08-b13",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Entry:</strong> Existing saved workspaces</p>",
                "id": "c08-b14",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "id": "c08-b15",
                "stages": [
                  {
                    "title": "User logs in → last-used workspace auto-opens (if no default set)",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Scans monitors, switches pages/workspaces as needed",
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Makes minor edits → auto-save or manual save persists state",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "journey",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Exit:</strong> Updated workspace state persisted for next session</p>",
                "id": "c08-b16",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c08",
            "title": "User Journeys",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Adoption & Activation",
                "id": "c09-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Is Workspace Valuable?</p>",
                "id": "c09-b2",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 2,
                "id": "c09-b3",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "% of active users who create ≥1 workspace within 7 days
Indicates initial value discovery",
                    "title": "Workspace Creation Rate",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "% of users who create a workspace, add ≥3 widgets & save it
Confirms meaningful usage, not just exploration",
                    "title": "Activation Rate",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "% of users using a template vs blank canvas
Validates usefulness of templates",
                    "title": "Template Usage Rate",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "% of users who abandon creation flow before saving
Identifies friction in workspace creation",
                    "title": "Creation Drop-off Rate",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
              {
                "body": "Engagement & Habit Formation",
                "id": "c09-b4",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Is It Becoming a Daily Tool?</p>",
                "id": "c09-b5",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 3,
                "id": "c09-b6",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "Workspace DAU ÷ Total DAU
Indicates daily stickiness",
                    "title": "Workspace DAU Ratio",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "% of sessions where Workspace opens by default
Signals habit formation",
                    "title": "Default Launch Rate",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Avg workspace sessions per user per day ÷ total sessions
Measures frequency of use",
                    "title": "Repeat Usage Rate",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Day-over-day retention for Workspace users
Validates long-term platform stickiness",
                    "title": "D1–D30 Retention",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Average widgets added per workspace
Indicates richness of setup",
                    "title": "Avg Widgets per Workspace",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "% of users switching pages within a session
Validates page-level value",
                    "title": "Page Switching Rate",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c09",
            "title": "Success Metrics",
          },
        ],
        "visuals": {
          "accent": "slate",
          "cover": {
            "mediaId": "cover-arcana-workspace",
          },
          "gallery": [],
          "hero": {
            "frame": "desktop",
            "start": "click",
            "type": "prototype",
            "url": "https://workspace-nu-liard.vercel.app/",
          },
        },
      },
      "publish": true,
      "slug": "arcana-workspace",
    },
    {
      "document": {
        "headlineOutcomeId": "o4",
        "outcomes": [
          {
            "id": "o1",
            "inStrip": true,
            "label": "Users currently losing >1 kg — baseline to improve",
            "type": "baseline",
            "value": "64%",
          },
          {
            "id": "o2",
            "inStrip": true,
            "label": "Additional loss for protocol followers vs non-followers",
            "type": "baseline",
            "value": "2.5kg",
          },
          {
            "id": "o3",
            "inStrip": true,
            "label": "Fitness MAU — structural engagement gap to close",
            "type": "baseline",
            "value": "25%",
          },
          {
            "id": "o4",
            "inStrip": false,
            "label": "lost by protocol followers",
            "type": "baseline",
            "value": "+2.5 kg",
          },
        ],
        "overview": {
          "company": "GLP Health",
          "kind": "study",
          "summary": "Repositioning a GLP app from activity tracker to outcome-driven metabolic platform for durable weight loss",
          "title": "GLP-1 digital scaffold",
          "topics": [
            "Engagement",
            "Personalization",
            "Monetization",
          ],
        },
        "schemaVersion": 1,
        "seo": {},
        "settings": {
          "redirectOldSlug": false,
        },
        "story": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>GLP-1 medications have redefined what is clinically possible in weight loss — but real-world outcomes remain fragile. The gap is no longer pharmacology; it is <strong>behavioral persistence, expectation management, and metabolic protection</strong>. Today's GLP app is optimised for <em>recording activity</em>, not <em>driving outcomes</em>.</p>",
                "id": "c01-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>The product does not help users <strong>interpret stalled progress</strong></li><li>The product does not help users <strong>understand body recomposition</strong></li><li>The product does not help users <strong>protect muscle mass</strong></li><li>The product does not help users <strong>stay adherent through plateaus and side effects</strong></li><li>As a result: only <strong>64% of users lose >1 kg</strong> · fitness engagement is <strong>~25% MAU</strong> · progress is perceived as binary ('weight down = success, else failure')</li><li>The next phase requires a strategic shift from <strong>tracking behaviour</strong> to <strong>owning outcomes</strong> — repositioning the GLP app as a <strong>Digital Scaffold</strong> that translates medication into durable metabolic outcomes.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c01-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c01",
            "title": "Summary",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "2.1 The GLP-1 Market Has Entered Its Second Act",
                "id": "c02-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>2022–2024 optimised for access:</strong> Rapid prescriber onboarding · Consumer-led demand · Medication-first value propositions</li><li><strong>2025–2026 structural shifts forcing a reset:</strong> Medication prices are falling · Prescription access is commoditising · 'GLP-only' platforms are losing defensibility</li><li><strong>Differentiation has moved downstream</strong> — from getting users on medication to ensuring outcomes persist.</li><li>Across Noom, Omada, Found, and HealthifyMe, a consistent pattern: <em>'Medication enables weight loss. Engagement architecture determines durability.'</em></li></ul>",
                "id": "c02-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "2.2 The Persistence Crisis Is the Real Bottleneck",
                "id": "c02-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Real-world GLP-1 programs show <strong>50–70% discontinuation within 12 months</strong>, with highest dropout in the <strong>first 90 days</strong>.</li><li>This is not due to lack of intent — it's due to unmanaged friction across <strong>The Attrition Triad</strong>:</li><li><strong>Biological:</strong> Nausea, GI distress, fatigue → Early dropout</li><li><strong>Psychological:</strong> Food identity shifts, stigma, confusion → Loss of confidence</li><li><strong>Metric:</strong> Scale plateaus despite fat loss → Motivation collapse</li><li>Most products fail because they treat weight loss as <strong>linear</strong>. Users experience it as <strong>non-linear, emotional, and confusing</strong>.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c02-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "2.3 What Winning Products Do Differently",
                "id": "c02-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Outcome visibility beats activity logging</strong> — Users need interpretation, not raw data.</li><li><strong>Human + digital hybrids outperform pure automation</strong> — Coaching access materially improves adherence and persistence.</li><li><strong>Muscle preservation is emerging as the new moat</strong> — Fast weight loss without muscle protection leads to metabolic slowdown and rebound.</li><li>This creates a clear opening: <em>The next category leader will sell <strong>metabolic integrity</strong>, not just weight loss.</em></li></ul>",
                "id": "c02-b6",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c02",
            "title": "Market Research: Why the Old Model Is Breaking",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>The End of 'Prescription as Product':</strong> As GLP-1 access becomes ubiquitous, users will ask harder questions. A logging-centric app cannot answer them. An outcome-owning product can. This is the inflection point where <strong>clinical ownership becomes the product</strong>.</p>",
                "id": "c03-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Does weight loss persist beyond 3 months?</li><li>Is muscle mass preserved?</li><li>Are side effects managed early?</li><li>Is cardiometabolic risk actually improving?</li></ul>",
                "id": "c03-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c03",
            "title": "Why Now",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "What's Working",
                "id": "c04-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Strong foundational tracking primitives (weight, meals, fitness, side effects)</li><li>High engagement with human coaches (~<strong>80% M2 chat usage</strong>)</li><li>Embedded clinical access</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Where the Experience Breaks",
                "id": "c04-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>No unified definition of 'progress'</li><li>Fitness treated as optional, not essential</li><li>Body composition invisible</li><li>Protocol adherence implicit, not explicit</li><li>Users log, but are not guided</li><li><em>The product records the journey — but does not <strong>direct</strong> it.</em></li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c04",
            "title": "Current Product Reality",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "5.1 Progress Feels Invisible",
                "id": "c05-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Users anchor success entirely to scale weight.</li><li>Users who lose ≥1 kg show <strong>–2 cm waist reduction</strong></li><li>Users who don't lose weight show <strong>+1 cm waist gain</strong></li><li>Waist tracking strongly correlates with perceived success</li><li>This does <strong>not</strong> imply waist logging causes weight loss. It shows that <strong>visible signals sustain motivation</strong> — and these signals need not be absolute weight loss.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "5.2 Expectation Mismatch With GLP-1",
                "id": "c05-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>User belief:</strong> 'Medication will do the work. I can eat anything freely.'</li><li><strong>Clinical reality:</strong> GLP-1 reduces appetite — not muscle loss risk.</li><li>Without guidance: Exercise drops · Lean mass declines · RMR falls · Weight regain risk increases</li><li>The app does not currently reset expectations early enough.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "5.3 Fitness Avoidance Is a Structural Risk",
                "id": "c05-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Fitness MAU ~25% · Majority complete only one session</li><li><strong>Clinical implication:</strong> Sarcopenic obesity risk · Unsustainable weight loss</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b6",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "5.4 Gender-Based Outcome Gap (New Insight)",
                "id": "c05-b7",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Men: <strong>1.66 kg</strong> average loss · Women: <strong>1.26 kg</strong> average loss</li><li><strong>Clinical context:</strong> Testosterone supports muscle preservation. Women require more intentional resistance training.</li><li><strong>Strategic implication:</strong> Fitness cannot be optional — especially for female users.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b8",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c05",
            "title": "Core User Pain Points (Data-Backed)",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>These are correlations, not causal claims. But they clearly indicate: when protocol adherence is understood and maintained, outcomes improve. <strong>Engagement clusters around success</strong> — not the other way around. The product must make adherence <strong>visible, actionable, and reinforced</strong>.</p>",
                "id": "c06-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Protocol followers lose <strong>~2.5 kg more</strong></li><li>Weight-loss cohort logs <strong>2× more meals</strong></li><li>Weight-loss cohort connects <strong>~30% more with doctors</strong></li><li>Non-weight-loss cohort shows <strong>waist gain</strong></li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c06",
            "title": "What the Data Is Actually Saying",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Pillar 1: Progress Visibility Beyond the Scale",
                "id": "c07-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Smart scale integration (where available)</li><li>Waist and measurement trends surfaced prominently</li><li>Full-body scan to visualise recomposition</li><li>Explicit plateau education</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Pillar 2: Muscle Preservation & Fitness as a Core Outcome",
                "id": "c07-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Resistance-first fitness programs</li><li>Proactive 1:1 fitness consultations</li><li>Clear framing: <em>fitness = metabolic protection</em></li><li>Gender-aware guidance (especially for women)</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Pillar 3: Clinical Adherence & Side-Effect Triage",
                "id": "c07-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Structured side-effect monitoring</li><li>Rapid escalation to coach/doctor</li><li>Dosage expectation education</li><li>Early-week intervention loops</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b6",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Pillar 4: Protocol-Driven Experience",
                "id": "c07-b7",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Clear weekly protocol</li><li>Visible adherence signals</li><li>Outcome-based milestones vs task completion</li></ul>",
                "id": "c07-b8",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c07",
            "title": "The Four Pillars of the GLP Digital Scaffold",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Primary Loop",
                "id": "c08-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Progress clarity → confidence → adherence → outcomes</strong></li></ul>",
                "id": "c08-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Secondary Loops",
                "id": "c08-b3",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Human accountability loop:</strong> Coach touchpoints at risk moments (plateau weeks, side-effect spikes) — not reactive support. Leverages existing ~80% M2 chat engagement.</li><li><strong>Visual reinforcement loop:</strong> Body scans, composition change visualisations, and waist trend charts shown contextually — where users are already looking.</li><li><strong>Safety loop:</strong> Side-effect resolution workflows that proactively surface guidance and escalation options. Trust built through managed adversity.</li><li>These loops align with industry evidence that <strong>hybrid human + digital models materially improve persistence</strong>.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c08-b4",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c08",
            "title": "Engagement & Retention Loops",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "Outcome Improvement",
                "id": "c09-b1",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Are users actually losing weight and keeping it off?</p>",
                "id": "c09-b2",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 2,
                "id": "c09-b3",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "64% baseline → 75% target
Primary outcome signal — closes the gap between medication efficacy and real-world results",
                    "title": "Users losing >1 kg",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Close from 2.5 kg to <1 kg vs non-followers
Protocol adherence is the primary causal lever",
                    "title": "Protocol followers weight gap",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": ">50% of active users logging waist measurements
Non-scale visibility drives motivation through plateaus",
                    "title": "Waist tracking adoption",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
              {
                "body": "Fitness & Muscle Protection",
                "id": "c09-b4",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Is the metabolic protection layer working?</p>",
                "id": "c09-b5",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 2,
                "id": "c09-b6",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "~25% baseline → 45% target
Structural engagement gap — fitness is medically essential, not optional",
                    "title": "Fitness MAU",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Users completing ≥3 sessions: <5% baseline → 20% target
Resistance training is the primary muscle preservation mechanism",
                    "title": "Resistance sessions/week",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Close the 0.4 kg gender outcome gap within 6 months
Gender-blind fitness experience fails the majority of the user base",
                    "title": "Female fitness engagement parity",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
              {
                "body": "Adherence & Retention",
                "id": "c09-b7",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Is the scaffold keeping users on protocol?</p>",
                "id": "c09-b8",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 2,
                "id": "c09-b9",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "30–50% baseline → 55% target
50–70% discontinuation is the core problem this entire strategy addresses",
                    "title": "12-month retention",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Reduce by 30%
Highest dropout in first 90 days — early intervention is highest leverage",
                    "title": "First-90-day dropout",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": ">80% escalation within 48hr of side-effect log
Rapid escalation converts biological friction into trust-building moments",
                    "title": "Coach escalation speed",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c09",
            "title": "Success Metrics",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>The GLP market is shifting from <strong>access to accountability</strong>. Products that remain logging-centric will struggle to differentiate. Platforms that <strong>own outcomes, expectations, and persistence</strong> will define the category.</p>",
                "id": "c10-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c10",
            "title": "Final Takeaway",
          },
        ],
        "visuals": {
          "accent": "green",
          "cover": {
            "mediaId": "cover-glp-1-digital-scaffold",
          },
          "gallery": [],
          "hero": {
            "type": "image",
          },
        },
      },
      "publish": true,
      "slug": "glp-1-digital-scaffold",
    },
    {
      "document": {
        "headlineOutcomeId": "o4",
        "outcomes": [
          {
            "id": "o1",
            "inStrip": true,
            "label": "Projected net incremental monthly revenue",
            "type": "projected",
            "value": "$50-65K",
          },
          {
            "id": "o2",
            "inStrip": true,
            "label": "ARPU target (from $2.00 baseline)",
            "type": "target",
            "value": "$2.10+",
          },
          {
            "id": "o3",
            "inStrip": true,
            "label": "Features across 4 player segments",
            "type": "output",
            "value": "5",
          },
          {
            "id": "o4",
            "inStrip": false,
            "label": "monthly revenue (~$50K)",
            "type": "projected",
            "value": "+5%",
          },
        ],
        "overview": {
          "company": "FarmVille 3 · Zynga",
          "kind": "study",
          "summary": "Pain-point-driven monetization via subscription, consumables, and community events to unlock 5% monthly incremental revenue",
          "title": "Revenue growth strategy",
          "topics": [
            "Monetization",
            "Mobile",
            "Games",
            "Engagement",
            "Retention",
          ],
        },
        "schemaVersion": 1,
        "seo": {},
        "settings": {
          "redirectOldSlug": false,
        },
        "story": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>FarmVille 3 generates ~$1M/month from ~500K MAU with two revenue drivers: direct IAP purchases and gem spending. The strategy targets <strong>$50K incremental monthly revenue (5% lift)</strong> via IAP-only mechanics without any ads or partnerships. Three progression bottlenecks are identified — sticker scarcity, tree fatigue, and exotic quest walls — and five features are proposed across four player segments, from a $2.99 subscription to community-driven competitive events.</p>",
                "id": "c01-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Current Revenue:</strong> ~$1M/month · <strong>Target Lift:</strong> +5% · <strong>Projected Net Impact:</strong> $50–65K/mo · <strong>ARPU Target:</strong> $2.10+</li><li><strong>Revenue Driver 1: Direct Purchase</strong> — Loot boxes, DLC, bundles bought with real money</li><li><strong>Revenue Driver 2: Gem Purchases</strong> — More gem spending = more real-money top-ups</li><li><strong>Approach:</strong> New ways to spend real money directly + increasing gem spending on in-game items — driven by solving real player frustrations, not adding more friction.</li></ul>",
                "id": "c01-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c01",
            "title": "Executive Summary",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>FarmVille 3 under-monetizes vs. farming genre leaders. Its animal breeding (gacha) mechanic is its unique strength — it creates a high completionist drive. But the same mechanic creates the highest frustration when stickers or exotic animals are gated. <strong>The opportunity is to reduce this friction for a price.</strong></p>",
                "id": "c02-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Competitive Benchmark",
                "id": "c02-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>FarmVille 3 vs. Farming Genre Leaders</p>",
                "id": "c02-b3",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 3,
                "id": "c02-b4",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "FarmVille 3: ~$1M · Hay Day: $15–20M · Township: $25–30M
FarmVille 3 is significantly under-monetized relative to MAU",
                    "title": "Est. Monthly Revenue",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "FarmVille 3: ~500K · Hay Day: 5–8M · Township: 10–15M
Smaller audience but comparable ARPU opportunity",
                    "title": "Est. MAU",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "FarmVille 3: $2.00 · Hay Day: $2.50–3.00 · Township: $2.00–2.50
Target is to close the ARPU gap to $2.10+ via pain-point monetization",
                    "title": "ARPU (Monthly)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "FarmVille 3: 2–3% · Hay Day: 3–5% · Township: 3–4%
Conversion gap is the primary revenue lever",
                    "title": "IAP Conversion Rate",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "FarmVille 3: Gems + Farm Pass · Hay Day: Diamonds + trading · Township: Events + content depth
Events and content depth are underutilized in FarmVille 3",
                    "title": "Primary Monetization",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "FarmVille 3: Animal gacha/breeding · Hay Day: No forced tutorial · Township: City + farm hybrid
Breeding mechanic is both the strength and the source of highest player frustration",
                    "title": "Key Differentiator",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c02",
            "title": "Market Context",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Spend-behavior segmentation reveals the real revenue levers: 400K 'Never Spent' players are the largest conversion pool, while 30K 'Frequent Buyers' offer the deepest ARPU expansion. A Level 35 player who has never spent is fundamentally different from a Level 20 who buys every pass — level-based segmentation misses this.</p>",
                "id": "c03-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Segment Profiles & Monetization Strategies",
                "id": "c03-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>4 Segments · Based on F2P Benchmarks (GameAnalytics 2024/2026)</p>",
                "id": "c03-b3",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 2,
                "id": "c03-b4",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "Play daily, social-heavy; never made a purchase
Convert via low-friction subscription ($2.99/mo) — largest conversion pool",
                    "title": "Never Spent (75–80% · ~400K)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Buy Farm Pass ($4.99) once or twice; use gems for level-ups
Increase spend frequency via contextual bundles + XP boosters",
                    "title": "Occasional Spender (12–15% · ~65K)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Spend on energy, time-skips, Sky Races; actively pursue exotic collections
Deepen progression spend via sticker bundles, breeding boosters, event passes",
                    "title": "Frequent Buyer (5–7% · ~30K)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Max out collections; buy every bundle; competitive status-driven
Create prestige spend via animal showoffs and exclusive community events",
                    "title": "Power Spender (1–2% · ~5K)",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c03",
            "title": "Player Segmentation",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Principle: Monetize the solution to player frustration, not the frustration itself.</strong></p>",
                "id": "c04-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "The Sticker Bottleneck",
                "id": "c04-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Players report extreme difficulty leveling up Farmhands due to rare sticker scarcity — the #1 complaint in app store reviews</li><li><strong>Opportunity:</strong> Sticker swap mechanics, targeted bundles</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Occasional Spenders & Frequent Buyers</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b3",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Tree Fatigue",
                "id": "c04-b4",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Trees wither after 3 harvests. Replacing costs coins/gems and high energy — creates negative friction that causes churn rather than spend</li><li><strong>Opportunity:</strong> Subscription that removes withering</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Never Spent & Occasional Spenders</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b5",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Exotic Quest Walls",
                "id": "c04-b6",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Many players are stuck on Chapter 10+ Exotic Quests because animal levels are too low — the gap feels unbridgeable</li><li><strong>Opportunity:</strong> Contextual bundles + breeding boosters</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Frequent Buyers & Power Spenders</li></ul>",
                "id": "c04-b7",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c04",
            "title": "Growth Levers: Three Pain Points = Three Opportunities",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>A subscription + two consumables target the largest untapped revenue pool. Projected combined revenue (net of 30% store cut): <strong>$30K–$43K/month</strong>.</p>",
                "id": "c05-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Farm Hand Club @ $2.99/month",
                "id": "c05-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Low-commitment entry below Farm Pass ($4.99) — priced to minimize friction for first-time buyers</li><li><strong>Infinite Tree Life</strong> — trees stop withering (solves #2 pain point)</li><li><strong>Weekly Sticker Swap</strong> — 3 dupes for 1 choice sticker (solves #1 pain point)</li><li><strong>+10% XP bonus</strong> on all farming activities</li><li>Exclusive 'Club Member' farm badge</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Never Spent (400K) → 3–4% conversion · <strong>Projected:</strong> $25K–$34K/mo net</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b3",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Farm Master Tonic (XP Booster)",
                "id": "c05-b4",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Consumable: doubles XP for 30 mins ($0.99) or 1 hr ($1.49)</li><li>Purchasable via gems OR real money (dual sink)</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Occasional Spenders — helps level up faster</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b5",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Lucky Charm Serum (Breed Boost)",
                "id": "c05-b6",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Applied during breeding: +30–40% rare animal chance</li><li>Priced at $1.49 / 30 gems per use</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Occasional & Frequent — collection psychology</li><li><strong>Combined XP Booster + Breed Boost projected:</strong> $5K–$9K/mo net</li></ul>",
                "id": "c05-b7",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c05",
            "title": "Solutions: Converting 'Never Spent' & Accelerating Progression",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Community events + showoffs + smart bundles capture the high-value segments. Projected combined revenue (net): <strong>$25K–$46K/month</strong>.</p>",
                "id": "c06-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Community Events",
                "id": "c06-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Great Harvest Day:</strong> Seasonal localized crops, leaderboards, milestone skins</li><li><strong>World Fair Day:</strong> Team co-op, mini-games, coin gambling for farm items</li><li>Monetization: Community Day Pass @ $2.99 · 4 events/month</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> All segments · <strong>Projected:</strong> $12K–$22K/mo net</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b3",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Animal Showoffs",
                "id": "c06-b4",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>Theme-Based Decoration:</strong> Seasonal packs (Christmas, Diwali) for animals — $1.99–$4.99</li><li><strong>Voting & Leaderboards:</strong> Weekly shows; players vote for best animal; winners get exclusive skins</li><li>Monetization: Entry fee 50 gems ($0.99) · Decoration packs $1.99–$4.99</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Frequent & Power Spenders · <strong>Projected:</strong> $8K–$14K/mo net</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b5",
                "type": "list",
              },
              {
                "body": "Contextual 'Missing Piece' Bundles",
                "id": "c06-b6",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li>Trigger: fail Exotic Quest 3× or hit Farmhand level cap</li><li>Bundle contains exact stickers/food needed to bridge the gap</li><li>Monetization: $1.99–$7.99 per bundle · 30-min purchase window</li><li><strong>Target:</strong> Frequent & Power Spenders · <strong>Projected:</strong> $5K–$10K/mo net</li></ul>",
                "id": "c06-b7",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c06",
            "title": "Solutions: Engagement, Social & Contextual Spend",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>All figures net of 30% Apple/Google store cut. Conservative scenario delivers 5.5% lift; moderate scenario delivers 8.9% lift.</p>",
                "id": "c07-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Initiative-Level Revenue Breakdown",
                "id": "c07-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Baseline: 500K MAU × $2.00 = $1.0M/mo → Target: $2.10 ARPU (+5%)</p>",
                "id": "c07-b3",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 3,
                "id": "c07-b4",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "Never Spent (400K) · 3–4% conv. · $25K–$34K net
+$0.05–$0.07 ARPU lift — biggest single lever",
                    "title": "Farm Hand Club ($2.99/mo)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Occasional (265K) · 2–3% conv. · $5K–$9K net
+$0.01–$0.02 ARPU lift",
                    "title": "XP Booster + Breed Boost",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "All active (500K) · 3–5% conv. · $12K–$22K net
+$0.02–$0.04 ARPU lift",
                    "title": "Community Events ($2.99)",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Frequent + Power (35K) · 15–20% conv. · $8K–$14K net
+$0.02–$0.03 ARPU lift",
                    "title": "Animal Showoffs",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Frequent + Power (35K) · 5–8% conv. · $5K–$10K net
+$0.01–$0.02 ARPU lift",
                    "title": "Contextual Bundles",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "$55K–$89K/month incremental
+$0.11–$0.18 ARPU · Conservative: 5.5% lift · Moderate: 8.9% lift",
                    "title": "TOTAL (net of 30% cut)",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c07",
            "title": "Financial Model: ARPU Bridge $2.00 → $2.10+",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p>Ship quick wins first, validate before investing in complex infrastructure. 10-week rollout: P0+P1 Ship (Wk 1–3) → P2 Sub Launch (Wk 3–5) → P3 Events Build (Wk 5–8) → P4 Showoffs + Full Rollout (Wk 8–10).</p>",
                "id": "c08-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "Feature Prioritization",
                "id": "c08-b2",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Ordered by Impact-to-Effort ratio</p>",
                "id": "c08-b3",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 3,
                "id": "c08-b4",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "Impact: $5–9K · Effort: Low
Fastest to validate; consumable pattern proven in category",
                    "title": "P0 · XP Booster + Breed Boost",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Impact: $5–10K · Effort: Low
Trigger logic on existing quest system — minimal new infra",
                    "title": "P1 · Contextual Bundles",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Impact: $25–34K · Effort: Med
Biggest single lever; creates recurring revenue base",
                    "title": "P2 · Farm Hand Club",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Impact: $12–22K · Effort: High
Highest engagement ceiling; needs event infrastructure",
                    "title": "P3 · Community Events",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Impact: $8–14K · Effort: High
Requires UGC system, voting, and moderation layer",
                    "title": "P4 · Animal Showoffs",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
              {
                "body": "Risk Register",
                "id": "c08-b5",
                "type": "heading",
              },
              {
                "body": "<p>Key risks and mitigations</p>",
                "id": "c08-b6",
                "style": "body",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "columns": 2,
                "id": "c08-b7",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "note": "A/B test Month 1
Add Premium tier ($7.99) if >15% downgrade observed",
                    "title": "Farm Pass cannibalization · MED",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "All items are progression aids or cosmetic
No competitive advantage — preserve fairness perception",
                    "title": "Pay-to-win perception · HIGH",
                  },
                  {
                    "note": "Cap 4 events/month
Monitor existing gem conversion 30 days post-launch",
                    "title": "Event fatigue / gem sink · MED",
                  },
                ],
                "type": "cards",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c08",
            "title": "Prioritization & Risks",
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "body": "<p><strong>Fix the pain, and the revenue follows.</strong></p>",
                "id": "c09-b1",
                "style": "lead",
                "type": "text",
              },
              {
                "body": "<ul><li><strong>01 · Ship P0/P1</strong> consumables + contextual bundles in Weeks 1–3 — validate spend appetite ($10–19K/mo net)</li><li><strong>02 · Launch Farm Hand Club</strong> ($2.99/mo) in Week 4 — biggest single lever at $25–34K/mo net, creates recurring revenue</li><li><strong>03 · Build Community Events + Animal Showoffs</strong> in parallel — highest engagement and social retention ceiling</li><li><strong>04 · Guard retention as a kill-switch</strong> — if D30 drops >2pp in any segment, pause and recalibrate immediately</li><li><strong>Success Metrics (30/60/90 Day):</strong> ARPU: $2.00 → $2.04 → $2.07 → $2.10+ · Conv. Rate: 2.5% → 3.0% → 3.5% · D30 Retention: No drop >2pp</li></ul>",
                "id": "c09-b2",
                "type": "list",
              },
            ],
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "c09",
            "title": "Recommendation",
          },
        ],
        "todo": [
          "prototype-link",
        ],
